hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16454","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit, he said: Ibn Umar narrated to me, from his father, from Umm Salama, that Abu Salama narrated to them that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When a calamity befalls one of you, let him say: Indeed we belong to Allah and indeed to Him we return. O Allah, with You I seek the reward of my calamity, so reward me in it and replace for me better than it. So when Abu Salama died, Allah left me behind in my family better than him."
"16455","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Layth, meaning Ibn Sa'd, narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Usama ibn al-Had, from Amr, meaning Ibn Abi Amr, from al-Muttalib, from Umm Salama, she said: Abu Salama came to me one day from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a saying that pleased me. He said: No calamity befalls one of the Muslims and he says istirja at his calamity, then says: O Allah, reward me in my calamity and leave for me better than it, except that is done for him. Umm Salama said: So I memorized that from him. Then when Abu Salama died I said istirja and said: O Allah, reward me in my calamity and leave me better than him. Then I returned to myself and said: From where will I have better than Abu Salama. Then when my waiting period ended, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sought permission to enter upon me while I was tanning a hide of mine, so I washed my hands of qaraz and gave him permission, and I placed for him a leather cushion stuffed with fiber, so he sat upon it and proposed to me. Then when he finished his speech I said: O Messenger of Allah, it is not that I have no desire for you, but I am a woman with intense jealousy, so I fear you may see from me something for which Allah will punish me, and I am a woman who has entered age, and I have dependents. So he said: As for what you mentioned of jealousy, Allah, Exalted and Majestic, will soon remove it from you. And as for what you mentioned of age, the like of what befell you has befell me. And as for what you mentioned of dependents, your dependents are my dependents. She said: So I submitted to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, married her. So Umm Salama said: Allah has replaced for me, in place of Abu Salama, better than him: the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
